# shadow-run needs NO credentials, API keys, or secrets to run — locally or
# deployed. lib/ (the simulation, reconciliation, and rollback engine) is
# deterministic and reads no external service; the plan's own risk section
# (E.1) requires this to stay true by construction — a grep-based
# architectural test, not a promise — once lib/simulate/** exists.
#
# The one environment variable a later, deployed milestone reads is set FOR
# you by Vercel — you never configure it yourself, and local dev works
# without it:
#
#   VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA   The SHA of the commit Vercel deployed. Read by
#                           app/api/health/route.ts (added at M2) to report
#                           which commit is live. Unset during `npm run dev`;
#                           the health check falls back to a local-dev value
#                           and still runs normally.
#
# There is nothing to fill in below. If a later milestone introduces a real
# credential, it gets documented here with what it's for when that happens —
# not invented ahead of time.
